    q("ml", "hard", ["validation"], "Why must you split time-series data by time instead of randomly, and how do you cross-validate it?", "A random split lets the model train on the future and test on the past, which leaks information. Use a time-ordered split and forward-chaining validation where each fold trains on earlier data and tests on later data.", ["Random split leaks the future", "Train on past, test on future", "Forward-chaining folds"], ["What else can leak in time-series features?"]),
